    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "The policy proposes tax incentives for new pharmacies and extra staff, but no independent costing of those incentives appears in the evidence, so it is impossible to judge whether the fiscal cost is offset by savings elsewhere. Until the tax relief is costed, the net effect on public finances cannot be determined.",
    "biggest_unknown": "The size of the tax-incentive revenue cost \u2014 and whether any resulting NHS savings (estimated only by an advocacy body) would offset it \u2014 is entirely unquantified in the provided evidence.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy offers tax incentives for new pharmacies and those employing more staff, alongside a Pharmacy First campaign.",
