      "notes": "Verdict is well-constructed and defensible. The too-uncertain direction is genuinely supported: tax-incentive revenue cost is unquantified in the evidence, the only savings figure (E3/NPA) is correctly flagged as advocacy-only, and the LSHTM evaluation is ongoing. Tier integrity holds \u2014 the \u00a3645m figure (E12) is correctly labelled measurable as it is a stated government investment figure, not a projection. The E27 claim/quote pairing is thin (the quote doesn't directly prove the tax incentive is uncosted, it notes existing searches focus elsewhere), but this is a warning-level observation at most and does not undermine the verdict, which is already grounded in the absence of evidence rather than leaning on E27 alone. Magnitude and time_horizon are both n/a consistent with too-uncertain. No party-blind or lever-leakage issues. No false balance concern \u2014 the uncertainty is genuine given the asymmetry between unquantified costs and advocacy-only savings estimates."
